    "q-221918": {
      "dom_id": "step-q221918",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe notation $8∤9$ means {{field-1}}. It is equivalent to the statement that {{field-2}}{{field-3}} $k,$ we have {{field-4}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The notation $a∤b$ means $a$ does not divides $b.$ So, $8∤9$ means $8\\text{ doesn't divide }9.$\n\nAccording to the definition of integer divisibility, the fact that $a$ does not divide $b$ means that for any integer $k,$ we have that \n\n$$\nb\\ne ak.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $8∤9$ is equivalent to the statement that $\\text{for any}$ $\\text{integer}$ $k,$ we have $9\\ne 8k.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
